{"jobs":[{"id":"5f3e320a-7324-4e69-9c49-78a9f4457cd9","title":"Full-Stack Engineer","department":"Engineering","team":"Engineering","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-10-10T22:42:46.897+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/5f3e320a-7324-4e69-9c49-78a9f4457cd9","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/5f3e320a-7324-4e69-9c49-78a9f4457cd9/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2><strong>About Big Leap</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Big Leap Health is democratizing access to breakthrough mental health treatments. We connect people with vetted clinics who provide treatments such as Spravato, TMS &amp; more covered by insurance.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">At Big Leap Health, we believe breakthrough mental health treatments are a pillar in the journey toward achieving our fullest potential but are often too expensive and inaccessible for most. We focus on making cutting-edge treatments like Spravato TMS, and other innovative therapies accessible to all through insurance coverage. These aren't just treatments; they're gateways to resilience, empathy, hope, and strength.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re building technology and tools to help clinics offer these treatments more easily, while enabling patients to use their insurance benefits to receive these life changing treatments. We’ve raised from top VCs and angels, are partnering with dozens of clinic operators, and are growing rapidly.<br /><br /></p><h2><strong>About The Role</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a <strong>Full-Stack Engineer</strong> in New York City (3-4 days/week in office) who thrives in a startup environment and knows how to ship.<br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">On a daily basis, you will build end-to-end workflows, take them to production, and solve real world problems across an out-sized scale. As an early technical steward, you will raise the bar for code quality and decision‑making, setting patterns that cement a world‑class engineering culture as we scale. While the company 10x’s, your scope and ownership will grow just as fast—building the tools, mental models, and platforms that let both you and Big Leap Health accelerate exponentially.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’ll work across the stack, from database schemas to UI components, and take full ownership of features from design through production deployment. The ideal candidate is someone whose built things end to end. You’ve worked at high-growth startups, kicked off your own side projects, or maybe indie hacked for a while. You know how to take high level requirements and run with them without getting lost in over-planning or scope creep.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You’re a generalist software engineer who is eager to take ownership, inclined to move quickly and hungry to ship high-impact software.</p><h2><br /><strong>Technologies We Use</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Different languages, frameworks, and databases,</strong> including React, Vue, Typescript, Node.js, PostgreSQL</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Industry-standard infrastructure,</strong> including Docker, AWS, Firebase, and Google Cloud</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2><strong>What We Value</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">An infinite learner. Someone who is relentless in their curiosity.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Partner-obsessed. Someone who deeply cares about delighting our customers and solving real pain points, not vanity metrics.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ultimate accountability while learning as a team, and both giving and receiving rapid feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Extreme empathy. Our customers are not tech companies. They are clinicians and practice managers who live and work in the real world. Empathy is critical to arriving at correct solutions.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Unafraid of failure. You take risks. You see failure as an opportunity to learn, grow, and be better the next time. In a weird way, you trick your brain into being excited when you fail, because it means you got a new opportunity to learn more.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>What We Require</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong coding skills with demonstrated proficiency in modern programming languages.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong engineering prowess, developed at start-ups.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with storage and data processing systems, cloud infrastructure, and other technical tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written and verbal communication skills and ability to iterate quickly with teammates, incorporating feedback and holding a high bar for quality.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Don’t Work Here</strong></h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Please don't join if you're not excited about:</p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Building an AI-enabled product for an industry rapidly growing and evolving</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Constantly talking to and visiting customers in the field</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Working in person with some of the most ambitious people in NYC</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Attempting to build a generational company, and the intensity required to do so</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>What We’re Looking For</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">4-7 years of experience building and shipping modern full-stack web applications.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience working at a VC-backed digital healthcare startup with the ability to move quickly, adapt priorities, and focus on outcomes over process.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Startup experience is preferred.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">A maker mindset. You’ve built side projects, indie apps, or internal tools from scratch and seen them through to launch.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited to work <strong>in person</strong> with a small, collaborative team in NYC.</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Why Join Us</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work with an ambitious team building meaningful technology that is transforming mental healthcare in our country</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ship quickly, own your work, and see your impact in production.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Modern stack, fast feedback loops, and a product-driven culture.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive pay, autonomy, and flexibility within a high-trust environment</p></li></ul><h2><br /><strong>Interview Process</strong></h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Intro call with Engineering</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founder Interview</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thought exercise, a two hour session and review with the team</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Team meeting (in-person)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Offer</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>You’ll also enjoy the following benefits:</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Industry-leading cash compensation for a startup of our stage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generous equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health, dental, and vision benefits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">New company Apple laptop</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$1,000 flexible home office budget</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a unique opportunity to join an early team of experienced healthcare operators.  If you’re excited by this, or the prospect of improving patient access to breakthrough mental health treatments, contact us!</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$160,000 - $200,000 a year</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation range for this position is $160,000 to $200,000, depending on experience; actual compensation will be dependent upon the specific role, location, as well as the individual’s qualifications, experience, skills and certifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Big Leap Health, we are an equal opportunity employer committed to a diverse, inclusive, and equitable workplace and candidate experience. We strive to create an environment where everyone has a sense of belonging and purpose, and where we learn from the unique experiences of those around us.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We encourage all qualified candidates to apply regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or family status, disability, gender, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or caregiver status, veteran status, or any other legally protected status.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT BIG LEAP\n\nBig Leap Health is democratizing access to breakthrough mental health treatments. We connect people with vetted clinics who provide treatments such as Spravato, TMS & more covered by insurance.\n\n\n\nAt Big Leap Health, we believe breakthrough mental health treatments are a pillar in the journey toward achieving our fullest potential but are often too expensive and inaccessible for most. We focus on making cutting-edge treatments like Spravato TMS, and other innovative therapies accessible to all through insurance coverage. These aren't just treatments; they're gateways to resilience, empathy, hope, and strength.\n\n\n\nWe’re building technology and tools to help clinics offer these treatments more easily, while enabling patients to use their insurance benefits to receive these life changing treatments. We’ve raised from top VCs and angels, are partnering with dozens of clinic operators, and are growing rapidly.\n\n\n\n\nABOUT THE ROLE\n\nWe’re looking for a Full-Stack Engineer in New York City (3-4 days/week in office) who thrives in a startup environment and knows how to ship.\n\n\nOn a daily basis, you will build end-to-end workflows, take them to production, and solve real world problems across an out-sized scale. As an early technical steward, you will raise the bar for code quality and decision‑making, setting patterns that cement a world‑class engineering culture as we scale. While the company 10x’s, your scope and ownership will grow just as fast—building the tools, mental models, and platforms that let both you and Big Leap Health accelerate exponentially.\n\n\n\nYou’ll work across the stack, from database schemas to UI components, and take full ownership of features from design through production deployment. The ideal candidate is someone whose built things end to end. You’ve worked at high-growth startups, kicked off your own side projects, or maybe indie hacked for a while. You know how to take high level requirements and run with them without getting lost in over-planning or scope creep.\n\n\n\nYou’re a generalist software engineer who is eager to take ownership, inclined to move quickly and hungry to ship high-impact software.\n\n\n\nTECHNOLOGIES WE USE\n\nDifferent languages, frameworks, and databases, including React, Vue, Typescript, Node.js, PostgreSQL\n\n\n\nIndustry-standard infrastructure, including Docker, AWS, Firebase, and Google Cloud\n\n\n\n\nWHAT WE VALUE\n\n - An infinite learner. Someone who is relentless in their curiosity.\n\n - Partner-obsessed. Someone who deeply cares about delighting our customers and solving real pain points, not vanity metrics.\n\n - Ultimate accountability while learning as a team, and both giving and receiving rapid feedback.\n\n - Extreme empathy. Our customers are not tech companies. They are clinicians and practice managers who live and work in the real world. Empathy is critical to arriving at correct solutions.\n\n - Unafraid of failure. You take risks. You see failure as an opportunity to learn, grow, and be better the next time. In a weird way, you trick your brain into being excited when you fail, because it means you got a new opportunity to learn more.\n\n\n\nWHAT WE REQUIRE\n\n - Strong coding skills with demonstrated proficiency in modern programming languages.\n\n - Strong engineering prowess, developed at start-ups.\n\n - Familiarity with storage and data processing systems, cloud infrastructure, and other technical tools.\n\n - Strong written and verbal communication skills and ability to iterate quickly with teammates, incorporating feedback and holding a high bar for quality.\n\n\n\nDON’T WORK HERE\n\nPlease don't join if you're not excited about:\n\n - Building an AI-enabled product for an industry rapidly growing and evolving\n\n - Constantly talking to and visiting customers in the field\n\n - Working in person with some of the most ambitious people in NYC\n\n - Attempting to build a generational company, and the intensity required to do so\n\n\n\nWHAT WE’RE LOOKING FOR\n\n - 4-7 years of experience building and shipping modern full-stack web applications.\n\n - Experience working at a VC-backed digital healthcare startup with the ability to move quickly, adapt priorities, and focus on outcomes over process.\n\n - Startup experience is preferred.\n\n - A maker mindset. You’ve built side projects, indie apps, or internal tools from scratch and seen them through to launch.\n\n - Excited to work in person with a small, collaborative team in NYC.\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN US\n\n - Work with an ambitious team building meaningful technology that is transforming mental healthcare in our country\n\n - Ship quickly, own your work, and see your impact in production.\n\n - Modern stack, fast feedback loops, and a product-driven culture.\n\n - Competitive pay, autonomy, and flexibility within a high-trust environment\n\n\n\nINTERVIEW PROCESS\n\n - Intro call with Engineering\n\n - Founder Interview\n\n - Thought exercise, a two hour session and review with the team\n\n - Team meeting (in-person)\n\n - Offer\n\n\n\n\nYOU’LL ALSO ENJOY THE FOLLOWING BENEFITS:\n\n - Industry-leading cash compensation for a startup of our stage\n\n - Generous equity\n\n - Health, dental, and vision benefits\n\n - New company Apple laptop\n\n - $1,000 flexible home office budget\n   \n   \n\nThis is a unique opportunity to join an early team of experienced healthcare operators.  If you’re excited by this, or the prospect of improving patient access to breakthrough mental health treatments, contact us!\n\n\n\n$160,000 - $200,000 a year\n\nCompensation range for this position is $160,000 to $200,000, depending on experience; actual compensation will be dependent upon the specific role, location, as well as the individual’s qualifications, experience, skills and certifications.\n\n\n\nAt Big Leap Health, we are an equal opportunity employer committed to a diverse, inclusive, and equitable workplace and candidate experience. We strive to create an environment where everyone has a sense of belonging and purpose, and where we learn from the unique experiences of those around us.\n\nWe encourage all qualified candidates to apply regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or family status, disability, gender, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or caregiver status, veteran status, or any other legally protected status.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$160K – $200K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$160K - $200K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"bc6b5ff6-8264-428e-b946-1a5ffd1a248c","tierSummary":"$160K – $200K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"b35638ab-e64f-4720-8d9e-fe6b8f4eed2e","summary":"$160K – $200K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":200000},{"id":"3a5b522c-e4fd-4c96-9104-aefbd0873081","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":160000,"maxValue":200000},{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"59f880c2-120a-4b6b-9570-2bb66077713a","title":"Payer Enrollment Specialist - Full Time","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States, Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2025-12-20T01:45:57.574+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/59f880c2-120a-4b6b-9570-2bb66077713a","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/59f880c2-120a-4b6b-9570-2bb66077713a/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Big Leap</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a fast-growing, multi-state medical &amp; behavioral clinician group dedicated to delivering high-quality outpatient and tele-health services focused on interventional mental health treatments (Spravato &amp; TMS). To keep pace with expansion, we’re adding an experienced Payer Enrollment Specialist to our remote operations team.<br /><br /></p><h2>Job Summary</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We’re looking for a proactive, detail-oriented team member to help keep our clinician payer enrollment process moving smoothly. In this role, you will play a key part in submitting payer enrollments, tracking enrollment statuses, following up with payers to identify and resolve blockers, and requesting fee schedules to support our operational planning. You’ll help ensure our clinicians get paneled quickly and stay on track, especially with plans in New York, New Jersey, California, Texas, Florida, Pennsylvania, and Colorado.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a great opportunity for someone who’s organized, persistent, and excited to dive into the fast-paced world of healthcare operations.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Key Responsibilities</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Submit new provider enrollments</strong> with Medicare, Medicaid, and major commercial payers (e.g., BCBS, UHC, Aetna, Cigna).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Proactively track </strong>provider enrollment and credentialing statuses<strong> </strong>with Medicare, Medicaid, and major commercial payers (e.g., BCBS, UHC, Aetna, Cigna).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Request and follow up on payer fee schedules to support internal planning.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain and update CAQH, PECOS, NPPES, and state portals; resolve discrepancies and follow-up requests quickly.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain up-to-date payer status logs; report in real time on turnaround times, expirations, and pending items utilizing our tracking tools.spreadsheet.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with credentialing team members and liaise with payer representatives to escalate issues, unblock delays, and shorten approval timelines.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Minimum Qualifications</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>2+ years’ recent, hands-on experience</strong> with payer enrollment.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Documented success credentialing providers with health plans in <strong>NY, NJ, CA, TX, FL, PA and CO</strong> (please list payers).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with credentialing databases, spreadsheets, and document-management tools.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written communication, follow-through, and problem-solving skills.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Preferred Qualifications</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience with payer enrollments for behavioral practices.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Schedule &amp; Compensation</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contract</strong> position averaging <strong>40 hours per week</strong>; additional hours available during peak cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Remote</strong>—work from anywhere in the U.S. (reliable high-speed internet required).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive hourly rate, commensurate with experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Why Join Us?</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work from anywhere in the US .</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consistent weekly workload.</p></li></ul><h2></h2>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT BIG LEAP\n\nWe are a fast-growing, multi-state medical & behavioral clinician group dedicated to delivering high-quality outpatient and tele-health services focused on interventional mental health treatments (Spravato & TMS). To keep pace with expansion, we’re adding an experienced Payer Enrollment Specialist to our remote operations team.\n\n\n\n\nJOB SUMMARY\n\nWe’re looking for a proactive, detail-oriented team member to help keep our clinician payer enrollment process moving smoothly. In this role, you will play a key part in submitting payer enrollments, tracking enrollment statuses, following up with payers to identify and resolve blockers, and requesting fee schedules to support our operational planning. You’ll help ensure our clinicians get paneled quickly and stay on track, especially with plans in New York, New Jersey, California, Texas, Florida, Pennsylvania, and Colorado.\n\nThis is a great opportunity for someone who’s organized, persistent, and excited to dive into the fast-paced world of healthcare operations.\n\n\n\n\nKEY RESPONSIBILITIES\n\n - Submit new provider enrollments with Medicare, Medicaid, and major commercial payers (e.g., BCBS, UHC, Aetna, Cigna).\n\n - Proactively track provider enrollment and credentialing statuses with Medicare, Medicaid, and major commercial payers (e.g., BCBS, UHC, Aetna, Cigna).\n\n - Request and follow up on payer fee schedules to support internal planning.\n\n - Maintain and update CAQH, PECOS, NPPES, and state portals; resolve discrepancies and follow-up requests quickly.\n\n - Maintain up-to-date payer status logs; report in real time on turnaround times, expirations, and pending items utilizing our tracking tools.spreadsheet.\n\n - Collaborate with credentialing team members and liaise with payer representatives to escalate issues, unblock delays, and shorten approval timelines.\n\n\n\n\nMINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - 2+ years’ recent, hands-on experience with payer enrollment.\n\n - Documented success credentialing providers with health plans in NY, NJ, CA, TX, FL, PA and CO (please list payers).\n\n - Fluency with credentialing databases, spreadsheets, and document-management tools.\n\n - Strong written communication, follow-through, and problem-solving skills.\n\n\n\n\nPREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS\n\n - Experience with payer enrollments for behavioral practices.\n\n\n\n\nSCHEDULE & COMPENSATION\n\n - Contract position averaging 40 hours per week; additional hours available during peak cycles.\n\n - Remote—work from anywhere in the U.S. (reliable high-speed internet required).\n\n - Competitive hourly rate, commensurate with experience.\n\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN US?\n\n - Work from anywhere in the US .\n\n - Consistent weekly workload.\n\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$22 – $28 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"328e0034-7005-4377-ae4e-0bbedba46570","tierSummary":"$22 – $28 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"1539d18a-d710-4371-a5b7-7d621fb89d9d","summary":"$22 – $28 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":22,"maxValue":28}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":22,"maxValue":28}]}},{"id":"f9862159-6db1-4993-bc42-f99e7c245434","title":"Payer Fee Schedule Specialist","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States, Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-05-05T18:30:22.904+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/f9862159-6db1-4993-bc42-f99e7c245434","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/f9862159-6db1-4993-bc42-f99e7c245434/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Us</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We are a fast-growing, multi-state medical and behavioral clinician group focused on interventional mental health treatments (Spravato and TMS). To support our expanding network of providers and payers, we're adding a detail-oriented Fee Schedule Specialist to our remote operations team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for an organized, persistent individual to own our payer fee schedule process end to end. You'll be responsible for submitting fee schedule requests to payers, following up until confirmed rates are received, and making sure the right CPT codes and provider details are captured at every step. You'll be a critical part of how our team plans financially and supports our clinician partners, which means accurate documentation and clear, timely communication are non-negotiables.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a great fit for someone who's comfortable picking up the phone, meticulous about the details, and knows how to get answers out of payer reps.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Submit fee schedule requests to Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payers (e.g., BCBS, UHC, Aetna, Cigna) across NY, NJ, CA, TX, FL, PA, CO, WI, WA, MD, and MO.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Follow up persistently with payer representatives by phone and email to obtain written copies of confirmed rates and resolve information gaps.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Verify that all requests include the correct CPT codes, provider NPIs, tax IDs, and any other payer-required identifiers to ensure accurate and timely fee schedule retrieval.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Log detailed, accurate status updates in our tracking systems in real time so the internal team always has current visibility.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flag discrepancies, missing rates, or unusual findings clearly, with enough context for the team to act.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Collaborate with credentialing and billing team members to prioritize requests and escalate stalled items.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Minimum Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">2+ years of hands-on experience in payer enrollment, credentialing, or revenue cycle operations with direct exposure to fee schedule requests.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Documented experience working with health plans in NY, NJ, CA, TX, FL, PA, CO, WI, WA, MD, and/or MO — please list payers in your application.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong oral communication skills for payer phone calls; confident navigating automated systems and reaching live representatives.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written communication skills for follow-up emails and internal status logging — your notes need to stand on their own.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Meticulous attention to detail, especially around CPT code sets and payer-specific data requirements.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluency with credentialing databases, spreadsheets, and document management tools.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Experience obtaining fee schedules for behavioral health or specialty practices (Spravato/esketamine, TMS, or similar).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Familiarity with payer portals.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Schedule and Compensation</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contract (1099)</strong> position averaging 15-20 hours per week; additional hours available during peak cycles.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Remote</strong> — work from anywhere in the U.S. (reliable high-speed internet required).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">$20.00 per hour, paid on a regular billing cycle.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Join Us</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible hours with a consistent weekly workload.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Growth potential into expanded operations or enrollment roles as the team scales.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Us\n\nWe are a fast-growing, multi-state medical and behavioral clinician group focused on interventional mental health treatments (Spravato and TMS). To support our expanding network of providers and payers, we're adding a detail-oriented Fee Schedule Specialist to our remote operations team.\n\nJob Summary\n\nWe're looking for an organized, persistent individual to own our payer fee schedule process end to end. You'll be responsible for submitting fee schedule requests to payers, following up until confirmed rates are received, and making sure the right CPT codes and provider details are captured at every step. You'll be a critical part of how our team plans financially and supports our clinician partners, which means accurate documentation and clear, timely communication are non-negotiables.\n\nThis is a great fit for someone who's comfortable picking up the phone, meticulous about the details, and knows how to get answers out of payer reps.\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n - Submit fee schedule requests to Medicare, Medicaid, and commercial payers (e.g., BCBS, UHC, Aetna, Cigna) across NY, NJ, CA, TX, FL, PA, CO, WI, WA, MD, and MO.\n\n - Follow up persistently with payer representatives by phone and email to obtain written copies of confirmed rates and resolve information gaps.\n\n - Verify that all requests include the correct CPT codes, provider NPIs, tax IDs, and any other payer-required identifiers to ensure accurate and timely fee schedule retrieval.\n\n - Log detailed, accurate status updates in our tracking systems in real time so the internal team always has current visibility.\n\n - Flag discrepancies, missing rates, or unusual findings clearly, with enough context for the team to act.\n\n - Collaborate with credentialing and billing team members to prioritize requests and escalate stalled items.\n\nMinimum Qualifications\n\n - 2+ years of hands-on experience in payer enrollment, credentialing, or revenue cycle operations with direct exposure to fee schedule requests.\n\n - Documented experience working with health plans in NY, NJ, CA, TX, FL, PA, CO, WI, WA, MD, and/or MO — please list payers in your application.\n\n - Strong oral communication skills for payer phone calls; confident navigating automated systems and reaching live representatives.\n\n - Strong written communication skills for follow-up emails and internal status logging — your notes need to stand on their own.\n\n - Meticulous attention to detail, especially around CPT code sets and payer-specific data requirements.\n\n - Fluency with credentialing databases, spreadsheets, and document management tools.\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Experience obtaining fee schedules for behavioral health or specialty practices (Spravato/esketamine, TMS, or similar).\n\n - Familiarity with payer portals.\n\nSchedule and Compensation\n\n - Contract (1099) position averaging 15-20 hours per week; additional hours available during peak cycles.\n\n - Remote — work from anywhere in the U.S. (reliable high-speed internet required).\n\n - $20.00 per hour, paid on a regular billing cycle.\n\nWhy Join Us\n\n - Flexible hours with a consistent weekly workload.\n\n - Growth potential into expanded operations or enrollment roles as the team scales.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$18 – $20 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"22cd2d00-7283-427d-8ba6-9fafcb77c531","tierSummary":"$18 – $20 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"c7bebc49-83f0-45e2-aef9-78cf268c84d9","summary":"$18 – $20 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":18,"maxValue":20}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":18,"maxValue":20}]}},{"id":"84e0c928-1267-452f-bc89-a673df0876e5","title":"Coding Specialist","department":"Operations","team":"Operations","employmentType":"Contract","location":"United States, Remote","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-07-20T19:56:18.773+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Remote","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"United States"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/84e0c928-1267-452f-bc89-a673df0876e5","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/84e0c928-1267-452f-bc89-a673df0876e5/application","descriptionHtml":"<p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>About Big Leap Health</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Big Leap Health’s mission is to transform access to mental healthcare by empowering clinics to easily launch and scale interventional psychiatry practices, specializing in cutting edge treatments such as Spravato (esketamine) and Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation (TMS). We're building a new standard of care by providing comprehensive operational, administrative, and clinical support, enabling psychiatrists to focus on delivering effective, life changing treatments.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Founded by industry leaders in mental health and healthcare technology, Big Leap Health is backed by top-tier investors and driven by a commitment to radically improving patient outcomes through innovative therapies. To keep pace with expansion, we're adding a Part Time Coding &amp; Audit Contractor to our remote operations team</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Join us in pioneering the future of mental health.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Job Summary</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're looking for a detail oriented contractor to help keep our claims accurate and our documentation audit ready. The core of this role is auditing coded claims against clinical documentation and catching the patterns that create compliance risk, things like unsupported add on codes, E/M mismatches, and template errors. Early on, you'll also do some direct coding as our internal coding tool is validated; that work tapers over time as the tool matures and auditing becomes the primary focus. You'll also support an annual MIPS/QPP eligibility review across our provider portfolio. Over time, this role will also take on payer audits as they come in.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">This is a strong fit for someone who's as comfortable reviewing and correcting coded output as they are producing it, and who can flag a documentation pattern clearly enough that a provider can actually act on it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Key Responsibilities</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Audit coded claims</strong> against underlying clinical documentation to identify unsupported codes, documentation gaps, and recurring errors.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Code claims directly</strong>, spending part of your time on direct coding work.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Flag documentation patterns</strong>, with enough specificity to support clinician facing compliance feedback.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Respond to payer audits</strong> as they come in, handling documentation requests and audit responses alongside our Head of RCM.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Support MIPS/QPP eligibility review</strong> for our provider portfolio.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Escalate unclear or exception cases rather than guessing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Maintain accurate records of audit findings and coding activity using our tracking tools.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><br /></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Minimum Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong, recent hands on experience with medical or behavioral health coding and auditing.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable auditing and correcting coded claims.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Strong written communication, able to explain a documentation issue clearly enough for a provider to fix it.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Reliable, self directed, and comfortable working independently.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Willingness to sign a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) and comply with HIPAA requirements for handling protected health information (PHI).</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred Qualifications</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Certification (CPC) is a plus but not required if experience is strong.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Behavioral health/psych coding background, especially E/M and psychotherapy coding.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Prior audit and compliance based experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Schedule &amp; Compensation</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Contract</strong> position, part-time, at <strong>10 to 15 hours per week</strong>.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible scheduling: contractor determines when and how work gets completed within weekly deliverables, with no set hours or shift requirement.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Remote</strong>, work from anywhere in the U.S. (reliable high speed internet required).</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Competitive hourly rate, commensurate with experience.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Why Join Us?</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Work from anywhere in the U.S.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Flexible, part time schedule.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Direct exposure to behavioral health coding across a multi-state, multi-specialty provider portfolio.</p></li></ul>","descriptionPlain":"About Big Leap Health\n\nBig Leap Health’s mission is to transform access to mental healthcare by empowering clinics to easily launch and scale interventional psychiatry practices, specializing in cutting edge treatments such as Spravato (esketamine) and Transcranial Magnetic Stimulation (TMS). We're building a new standard of care by providing comprehensive operational, administrative, and clinical support, enabling psychiatrists to focus on delivering effective, life changing treatments.\n\n\n\nFounded by industry leaders in mental health and healthcare technology, Big Leap Health is backed by top-tier investors and driven by a commitment to radically improving patient outcomes through innovative therapies. To keep pace with expansion, we're adding a Part Time Coding & Audit Contractor to our remote operations team\n\n\n\nJoin us in pioneering the future of mental health.\n\n\n\nJob Summary\n\nWe're looking for a detail oriented contractor to help keep our claims accurate and our documentation audit ready. The core of this role is auditing coded claims against clinical documentation and catching the patterns that create compliance risk, things like unsupported add on codes, E/M mismatches, and template errors. Early on, you'll also do some direct coding as our internal coding tool is validated; that work tapers over time as the tool matures and auditing becomes the primary focus. You'll also support an annual MIPS/QPP eligibility review across our provider portfolio. Over time, this role will also take on payer audits as they come in.\n\n\n\nThis is a strong fit for someone who's as comfortable reviewing and correcting coded output as they are producing it, and who can flag a documentation pattern clearly enough that a provider can actually act on it.\n\n\n\nKey Responsibilities\n\n - Audit coded claims against underlying clinical documentation to identify unsupported codes, documentation gaps, and recurring errors.\n\n - Code claims directly, spending part of your time on direct coding work.\n\n - Flag documentation patterns, with enough specificity to support clinician facing compliance feedback.\n\n - Respond to payer audits as they come in, handling documentation requests and audit responses alongside our Head of RCM.\n\n - Support MIPS/QPP eligibility review for our provider portfolio.\n\n - Escalate unclear or exception cases rather than guessing.\n\n - Maintain accurate records of audit findings and coding activity using our tracking tools.\n\n\n\n\nMinimum Qualifications\n\n - Strong, recent hands on experience with medical or behavioral health coding and auditing.\n\n - Comfortable auditing and correcting coded claims.\n\n - Strong written communication, able to explain a documentation issue clearly enough for a provider to fix it.\n\n - Reliable, self directed, and comfortable working independently.\n\n - Willingness to sign a Business Associate Agreement (BAA) and comply with HIPAA requirements for handling protected health information (PHI).\n\n\n\nPreferred Qualifications\n\n - Certification (CPC) is a plus but not required if experience is strong.\n\n - Behavioral health/psych coding background, especially E/M and psychotherapy coding.\n\n - Prior audit and compliance based experience.\n\n\n\nSchedule & Compensation\n\n - Contract position, part-time, at 10 to 15 hours per week.\n\n - Flexible scheduling: contractor determines when and how work gets completed within weekly deliverables, with no set hours or shift requirement.\n\n - Remote, work from anywhere in the U.S. (reliable high speed internet required).\n\n - Competitive hourly rate, commensurate with experience.\n\n\n\nWhy Join Us?\n\n - Work from anywhere in the U.S.\n\n - Flexible, part time schedule.\n\n - Direct exposure to behavioral health coding across a multi-state, multi-specialty provider portfolio.","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$25 – $31 per hour","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":null,"compensationTiers":[{"id":"80c31fcb-39d6-4e23-98b5-43dd36e0fe2e","tierSummary":"$25 – $31 per hour","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"f92e7361-62cb-437d-8321-21fececea1cc","summary":"$25 – $31 per hour","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":25,"maxValue":31}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 HOUR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":25,"maxValue":31}]}},{"id":"458967f1-a4b0-4e83-aae7-bcfaa8d3e346","title":"Strategy and Operations Lead","department":"Office of CEO","team":"Office of CEO","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-26T23:41:08.512+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":true,"workplaceType":"Hybrid","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/458967f1-a4b0-4e83-aae7-bcfaa8d3e346","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/458967f1-a4b0-4e83-aae7-bcfaa8d3e346/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Big Leap Health</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Big Leap Health is transforming how interventional psychiatry practices deliver care. We partner with clinics across the country to power TMS and Spravato services — combining clinical expertise, technology, and payer integration to make high-quality mental healthcare more accessible. These aren't just treatments; they're gateways to resilience, empathy, hope, and strength.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building the infrastructure layer for the next generation of in-person behavioral health, replacing administrative chaos with a connected, data-driven operating system that helps practices focus on what matters: patients.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised $10M+ from top VCs and angels, have dozens of customers across the country and are rapidly growing.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're starting a Strategy &amp; Ops function, and this is the person who gets to define it.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to the CEO and work on whatever matters most that month. Some weeks that means running our planning cadence and getting the leadership team aligned on the quarter; other weeks you're on the phone with a payer's network team, recruiting clinicians onto our medical advisory board, rebuilding how we run outbound, or picking up a project nobody else has time to own. The through-line is judgment, not a functional specialty.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll get problems with no playbook and be expected to come back with a recommendation, the reasoning behind it, and a plan you can run yourself. As the function grows, this seat may pick up direct reports; we'd want whoever's in it to build that team.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good fit if you'd rather own an outcome than a workstream, and if you want to see up close how a healthcare technology company actually scales.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Example Projects</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run the offsite that sets next quarter's OKRs, then own the weekly and monthly rhythm that keeps them from quietly dying six weeks later, including a company-wide update people actually read</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take the medical advisory board from idea to first meeting. Identify the interventional psychiatry KOLs worth having, get them to say yes</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Rebuild the financial model against what our operations actually taught us, then tell us where our unit economics and pricing are wrong</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Evaluate our GTM motion and improve our sales process to drive better velocity and outcomes</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>About You</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">6–10 years of full-time experience, including real time at a fast-growing, VC-backed early-stage startup</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Analytical by instinct. You can build a model in Sheets from ugly source data and defend every assumption in it. You don't need to be a data scientist; you do need to be the person who checks a number before repeating it</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You turn ambiguity into a plan quickly, and then execute the plan</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Comfortable in outside conversations, whether that's a payer's network director, a skeptical psychiatrist, or a clinic owner who is frustrated with the system</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Writes and presents well: a board memo in the morning, a payer pitch that afternoon</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership mentality, entrepreneurial instincts, and a real sense of urgency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent in the modern AI stack (you know the difference between an MCP and a Claude Skill, or you can show us what you've built with something else)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Digital health experience, or a track record of learning an unfamiliar sector in weeks</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Genuinely interested in where breakthrough mental healthcare treatment is heading</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thrives in a fast-paced, high-performance culture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited to work in a hybrid work environment in the NYC area (3+ days in-person required)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred:</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Digital healthcare startup experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Consulting, banking, or investing background paired with at least one operating role</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to payer contracting, reimbursement, or revenue cycle management</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Has managed or mentored junior teammates</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Why Join Us</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Transform Mental Health in the US:</strong> We are at the forefront of democratizing access to breakthrough mental healthcare treatments in this country, and you'll have a front row seat.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Culture of Excellence:</strong> Our leadership team has decades of experience at successful VC backed startups with several exits, and we're devoted to applying lessons learned to transforming mental health treatment for those most in need.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Apprenticeship &amp; Coaching:</strong> We expect all our early hires to grow into leaders in our company and the industry, and we are committed to helping you get there.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Joining the Ground Floor:</strong> This is an opportunity to join the next stage of growth for a company that is democratizing access to a rapidly evolving field of healthcare that is transforming mental health across the country.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll also enjoy the following benefits:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Industry-leading cash compensation for a startup of our stage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generous equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health, dental, and vision benefits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">New Macbook + modern software stack (Airtable, Notion, Slack, etc.)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$140,000 - $190,000 a year + bonus</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation range for this position is $140,000 to $190,000 + discretionary bonus, depending on experience; actual compensation will be dependent upon the specific role, location, as well as the individual's qualifications, experience, skills and certifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Big Leap Health, we are an equal opportunity employer committed to a diverse, inclusive, and equitable workplace and candidate experience. We strive to create an environment where everyone has a sense of belonging and purpose, and where we learn from the unique experiences of those around us.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We encourage all qualified candidates to apply regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or family status, disability, gender, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or caregiver status, veteran status, or any other legally protected status.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT BIG LEAP HEALTH\n\nBig Leap Health is transforming how interventional psychiatry practices deliver care. We partner with clinics across the country to power TMS and Spravato services — combining clinical expertise, technology, and payer integration to make high-quality mental healthcare more accessible. These aren't just treatments; they're gateways to resilience, empathy, hope, and strength.\n\n\n\nWe're building the infrastructure layer for the next generation of in-person behavioral health, replacing administrative chaos with a connected, data-driven operating system that helps practices focus on what matters: patients.\n\n\n\nWe've raised $10M+ from top VCs and angels, have dozens of customers across the country and are rapidly growing.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nWe're starting a Strategy & Ops function, and this is the person who gets to define it.\n\n\n\nYou'll report to the CEO and work on whatever matters most that month. Some weeks that means running our planning cadence and getting the leadership team aligned on the quarter; other weeks you're on the phone with a payer's network team, recruiting clinicians onto our medical advisory board, rebuilding how we run outbound, or picking up a project nobody else has time to own. The through-line is judgment, not a functional specialty.\n\n\n\nYou'll get problems with no playbook and be expected to come back with a recommendation, the reasoning behind it, and a plan you can run yourself. As the function grows, this seat may pick up direct reports; we'd want whoever's in it to build that team.\n\n\n\nGood fit if you'd rather own an outcome than a workstream, and if you want to see up close how a healthcare technology company actually scales.\n\n\n\n\nEXAMPLE PROJECTS\n\n - Run the offsite that sets next quarter's OKRs, then own the weekly and monthly rhythm that keeps them from quietly dying six weeks later, including a company-wide update people actually read\n\n - Take the medical advisory board from idea to first meeting. Identify the interventional psychiatry KOLs worth having, get them to say yes\n\n - Rebuild the financial model against what our operations actually taught us, then tell us where our unit economics and pricing are wrong\n\n - Evaluate our GTM motion and improve our sales process to drive better velocity and outcomes\n\n\n\n\nABOUT YOU\n\n - 6–10 years of full-time experience, including real time at a fast-growing, VC-backed early-stage startup\n\n - Analytical by instinct. You can build a model in Sheets from ugly source data and defend every assumption in it. You don't need to be a data scientist; you do need to be the person who checks a number before repeating it\n\n - You turn ambiguity into a plan quickly, and then execute the plan\n\n - Comfortable in outside conversations, whether that's a payer's network director, a skeptical psychiatrist, or a clinic owner who is frustrated with the system\n\n - Writes and presents well: a board memo in the morning, a payer pitch that afternoon\n\n - Ownership mentality, entrepreneurial instincts, and a real sense of urgency\n\n - Fluent in the modern AI stack (you know the difference between an MCP and a Claude Skill, or you can show us what you've built with something else)\n\n - Digital health experience, or a track record of learning an unfamiliar sector in weeks\n\n - Genuinely interested in where breakthrough mental healthcare treatment is heading\n\n - Thrives in a fast-paced, high-performance culture\n\n - Excited to work in a hybrid work environment in the NYC area (3+ days in-person required)\n\n\n\nPreferred:\n\n - Digital healthcare startup experience\n\n - Consulting, banking, or investing background paired with at least one operating role\n\n - Exposure to payer contracting, reimbursement, or revenue cycle management\n\n - Has managed or mentored junior teammates\n\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN US\n\n - Transform Mental Health in the US: We are at the forefront of democratizing access to breakthrough mental healthcare treatments in this country, and you'll have a front row seat.\n\n - Culture of Excellence: Our leadership team has decades of experience at successful VC backed startups with several exits, and we're devoted to applying lessons learned to transforming mental health treatment for those most in need.\n\n - Strong Apprenticeship & Coaching: We expect all our early hires to grow into leaders in our company and the industry, and we are committed to helping you get there.\n\n - Joining the Ground Floor: This is an opportunity to join the next stage of growth for a company that is democratizing access to a rapidly evolving field of healthcare that is transforming mental health across the country.\n\n\n\nYou'll also enjoy the following benefits:\n\n\n\n - Industry-leading cash compensation for a startup of our stage\n\n - Generous equity\n\n - Health, dental, and vision benefits\n\n - New Macbook + modern software stack (Airtable, Notion, Slack, etc.)\n\n\n\n$140,000 - $190,000 a year + bonus\n\n\n\nCompensation range for this position is $140,000 to $190,000 + discretionary bonus, depending on experience; actual compensation will be dependent upon the specific role, location, as well as the individual's qualifications, experience, skills and certifications.\n\n\n\nAt Big Leap Health, we are an equal opportunity employer committed to a diverse, inclusive, and equitable workplace and candidate experience. We strive to create an environment where everyone has a sense of belonging and purpose, and where we learn from the unique experiences of those around us.\n\n\n\nWe encourage all qualified candidates to apply regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or family status, disability, gender, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or caregiver status, veteran status, or any other legally protected status.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$140K – $190K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$140K - $190K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"296fa614-127d-41a1-8ce8-8fa784abb7bb","tierSummary":"$140K – $190K • Offers Equity • Offers Bonus","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"82d4928b-e859-4aa2-a44a-16264231bade","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"1226d344-337e-457a-8177-ba4d93cbb9d9","summary":"$140K – $190K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":140000,"maxValue":190000},{"id":"5e473686-2aa3-4aa1-afc1-cc6a9780a98d","summary":"Offers Bonus","compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":140000,"maxValue":190000},{"compensationType":"Bonus","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":null,"maxValue":null}]}},{"id":"671a061d-21e4-45de-9ea0-c745440d0c65","title":"Strategy and Operations Associate","department":"Office of CEO","team":"Office of CEO","employmentType":"FullTime","location":"New York City","shouldDisplayCompensationOnJobPostings":true,"secondaryLocations":[],"publishedAt":"2026-08-05T23:00:18.190+00:00","isListed":true,"isRemote":false,"workplaceType":"OnSite","address":{"postalAddress":{"addressRegion":"New York","addressCountry":"United States","addressLocality":"New York City"}},"jobUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/671a061d-21e4-45de-9ea0-c745440d0c65","applyUrl":"https://jobs.ashbyhq.com/big-leap-health/671a061d-21e4-45de-9ea0-c745440d0c65/application","descriptionHtml":"<h2>About Big Leap Health</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Big Leap Health is transforming how interventional psychiatry practices deliver care. We partner with clinics across the country to power TMS and Spravato® services — combining clinical expertise, technology, and payer integration to make high-quality mental healthcare more accessible. These aren't just treatments; they're gateways to resilience, empathy, hope, and strength.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We're building the infrastructure layer for the next generation of in-person behavioral health, replacing administrative chaos with a connected, data-driven operating system that helps practices focus on what matters: patients.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">We've raised $10M+ from top VCs and angels, have dozens of customers across the country and are rapidly growing.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>The Role</h2><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll report to the CEO and work day to day alongside our Strategy &amp; Ops Lead. Most weeks you're doing the analysis behind a decision someone is about to make, running an outbound or campaign experiment, researching payers and prospects, or keeping the planning rhythm on track. Then there are the things that land on a Tuesday and need to ship by Friday, and you'll own plenty of those.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>What You'll Own</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The weekly metrics pack and the dashboards under it, plus the exhibits that go into board and investor reporting</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The mechanics of our operating cadence: OKR tracking, agendas and prep for leadership meetings, company updates, and making sure last week's commitments actually happened</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Execution on growth: prospect and target research, list building, outbound sequences, campaign setup, CRM hygiene, and the pipeline reporting that tells us whether any of it worked</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Research and legwork behind payer outreach and our medical advisory board, from sourcing and first-touch through scheduling and materials</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">The analysis behind real decisions: clinic ramp and retention, funnel conversion, unit economics, pricing scenarios</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Example Projects</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Get us to one version of visits, revenue, and clinic performance that nobody argues about, then turn it into the weekly pack the leadership team runs on</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Run an outbound experiment start to finish: build the target list, write the sequences, launch it, and come back with what actually converted and what you'd do next</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Build the payer research file. Who covers TMS and Spravato in our markets, at what rates, and what it would take to get in front of them, then get the first meetings on the calendar</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Take a process that only works because someone remembers to run it, like clinic onboarding or the credentialing tracker, and rebuild it so it runs without them</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>About You</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">3–5 years of full-time experience, including at least one stretch somewhere fast and demanding (startup ops or strategy, consulting, banking, private equity, growth or BizOps)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Good with numbers. Messy data in, clean analysis out, explained without a walkthrough.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Precise, and you close loops without being chased</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Writes clearly enough to put a recommendation in front of the CEO and have it hold up</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fine working before the process exists, and inclined to write the process down afterward</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Fluent in the modern AI stack (you know the difference between an MCP and a Claude Skill, or you can show us what you've built with something else)</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Ownership mentality and a real sense of urgency</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Curious about digital health, and interested in where interventional psychiatry is heading</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Thrives in a fast-paced, high-performance culture</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Excited to work in a hybrid work environment in the NYC area (3+ days in-person required)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Preferred</strong></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Digital healthcare startup experience</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Exposure to sales, marketing, or revenue operations</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Builds comfortably in modern tooling (Airtable, Notion, CRM, BI, light scripting or AI tools)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><h2>Why Join Us</h2><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Transform Mental Health in the US:</strong> We are at the forefront of democratizing access to breakthrough mental healthcare treatments in this country, and you'll have a front row seat.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Culture of Excellence:</strong> Our leadership team has decades of experience at successful VC backed startups with several exits, and we're devoted to applying lessons learned to transforming mental health treatment for those most in need.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Strong Apprenticeship &amp; Coaching:</strong> We expect all our early hires to grow into leaders in our company and the industry, and we are committed to helping you get there.</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>Joining the Ground Floor:</strong> This is an opportunity to join the next stage of growth for a company that is democratizing access to a rapidly evolving field of healthcare that is transforming mental health across the country.</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">You'll also enjoy the following benefits:</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><ul style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Industry-leading cash compensation for a startup of our stage</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Generous equity</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Health, dental, and vision benefits</p></li><li><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">New Macbook + modern software stack (Airtable, Notion, Slack, etc.)</p></li></ul><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><strong>$100,000 - $130,000 a year</strong></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\">Compensation range for this position is $100,000 to $130,000, depending on experience; actual compensation will be dependent upon the specific role, location, as well as the individual's qualifications, experience, skills and certifications.</p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>At Big Leap Health, we are an equal opportunity employer committed to a diverse, inclusive, and equitable workplace and candidate experience. We strive to create an environment where everyone has a sense of belonging and purpose, and where we learn from the unique experiences of those around us.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"><em>We encourage all qualified candidates to apply regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or family status, disability, gender, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or caregiver status, veteran status, or any other legally protected status.</em></p><p style=\"min-height:1.5em\"></p>","descriptionPlain":"ABOUT BIG LEAP HEALTH\n\nBig Leap Health is transforming how interventional psychiatry practices deliver care. We partner with clinics across the country to power TMS and Spravato® services — combining clinical expertise, technology, and payer integration to make high-quality mental healthcare more accessible. These aren't just treatments; they're gateways to resilience, empathy, hope, and strength.\n\n\n\nWe're building the infrastructure layer for the next generation of in-person behavioral health, replacing administrative chaos with a connected, data-driven operating system that helps practices focus on what matters: patients.\n\n\n\nWe've raised $10M+ from top VCs and angels, have dozens of customers across the country and are rapidly growing.\n\n\n\n\nTHE ROLE\n\nYou'll report to the CEO and work day to day alongside our Strategy & Ops Lead. Most weeks you're doing the analysis behind a decision someone is about to make, running an outbound or campaign experiment, researching payers and prospects, or keeping the planning rhythm on track. Then there are the things that land on a Tuesday and need to ship by Friday, and you'll own plenty of those.\n\n\n\n\nWHAT YOU'LL OWN\n\n - The weekly metrics pack and the dashboards under it, plus the exhibits that go into board and investor reporting\n\n - The mechanics of our operating cadence: OKR tracking, agendas and prep for leadership meetings, company updates, and making sure last week's commitments actually happened\n\n - Execution on growth: prospect and target research, list building, outbound sequences, campaign setup, CRM hygiene, and the pipeline reporting that tells us whether any of it worked\n\n - Research and legwork behind payer outreach and our medical advisory board, from sourcing and first-touch through scheduling and materials\n\n - The analysis behind real decisions: clinic ramp and retention, funnel conversion, unit economics, pricing scenarios\n\n\n\n\nEXAMPLE PROJECTS\n\n - Get us to one version of visits, revenue, and clinic performance that nobody argues about, then turn it into the weekly pack the leadership team runs on\n\n - Run an outbound experiment start to finish: build the target list, write the sequences, launch it, and come back with what actually converted and what you'd do next\n\n - Build the payer research file. Who covers TMS and Spravato in our markets, at what rates, and what it would take to get in front of them, then get the first meetings on the calendar\n\n - Take a process that only works because someone remembers to run it, like clinic onboarding or the credentialing tracker, and rebuild it so it runs without them\n\n\n\n\nABOUT YOU\n\n - 3–5 years of full-time experience, including at least one stretch somewhere fast and demanding (startup ops or strategy, consulting, banking, private equity, growth or BizOps)\n\n - Good with numbers. Messy data in, clean analysis out, explained without a walkthrough.\n\n - Precise, and you close loops without being chased\n\n - Writes clearly enough to put a recommendation in front of the CEO and have it hold up\n\n - Fine working before the process exists, and inclined to write the process down afterward\n\n - Fluent in the modern AI stack (you know the difference between an MCP and a Claude Skill, or you can show us what you've built with something else)\n\n - Ownership mentality and a real sense of urgency\n\n - Curious about digital health, and interested in where interventional psychiatry is heading\n\n - Thrives in a fast-paced, high-performance culture\n\n - Excited to work in a hybrid work environment in the NYC area (3+ days in-person required)\n\n\n\nPreferred\n\n - Digital healthcare startup experience\n\n - Exposure to sales, marketing, or revenue operations\n\n - Builds comfortably in modern tooling (Airtable, Notion, CRM, BI, light scripting or AI tools)\n\n\n\n\nWHY JOIN US\n\n - Transform Mental Health in the US: We are at the forefront of democratizing access to breakthrough mental healthcare treatments in this country, and you'll have a front row seat.\n\n - Culture of Excellence: Our leadership team has decades of experience at successful VC backed startups with several exits, and we're devoted to applying lessons learned to transforming mental health treatment for those most in need.\n\n - Strong Apprenticeship & Coaching: We expect all our early hires to grow into leaders in our company and the industry, and we are committed to helping you get there.\n\n - Joining the Ground Floor: This is an opportunity to join the next stage of growth for a company that is democratizing access to a rapidly evolving field of healthcare that is transforming mental health across the country.\n\n\n\nYou'll also enjoy the following benefits:\n\n\n\n - Industry-leading cash compensation for a startup of our stage\n\n - Generous equity\n\n - Health, dental, and vision benefits\n\n - New Macbook + modern software stack (Airtable, Notion, Slack, etc.)\n\n\n\n$100,000 - $130,000 a year\n\n\n\nCompensation range for this position is $100,000 to $130,000, depending on experience; actual compensation will be dependent upon the specific role, location, as well as the individual's qualifications, experience, skills and certifications.\n\n\n\nAt Big Leap Health, we are an equal opportunity employer committed to a diverse, inclusive, and equitable workplace and candidate experience. We strive to create an environment where everyone has a sense of belonging and purpose, and where we learn from the unique experiences of those around us.\n\n\n\nWe encourage all qualified candidates to apply regardless of race, color, ancestry, religion, national origin, sexual orientation, age, citizenship, marital or family status, disability, gender, gender identity or expression, pregnancy or caregiver status, veteran status, or any other legally protected status.\n\n","compensation":{"compensationTierSummary":"$100K – $130K • Offers Equity","scrapeableCompensationSalarySummary":"$100K - $130K","compensationTiers":[{"id":"f12b89b5-8aa0-4efd-9e75-c21903a5e19b","tierSummary":"$100K – $130K • Offers Equity","title":null,"additionalInformation":null,"components":[{"id":"ea3e3579-b825-42e8-bc5d-4e7e66536b99","summary":"Offers Equity","compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"id":"18a96c8f-a8f7-4347-8597-b0a133a6fbc6","summary":"$100K – $130K","compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":130000}]}],"summaryComponents":[{"compensationType":"EquityPercentage","interval":"NONE","currencyCode":null,"minValue":null,"maxValue":null},{"compensationType":"Salary","interval":"1 YEAR","currencyCode":"USD","minValue":100000,"maxValue":130000}]}}],"apiVersion":"1"}